WEBVTT

00:01.290 --> 00:04.800
<i>My dad finally saw me
for who I truly am.</i>

00:05.050 --> 00:06.670
<i>His daughter Eva.</i>

00:07.220 --> 00:08.680
<i>Don Wei went through
a lot of trouble</i>

00:08.840 --> 00:11.850
<i>to justify why he had
abandoned me after Mom's crash.</i>

00:12.050 --> 00:12.850
Whatever.

00:13.010 --> 00:16.100
<i>In the end,
he still abandoned me.</i>

00:16.430 --> 00:18.600
<i>Winning the Ultimate Prize
is the only way</i>

00:18.940 --> 00:21.900
<i>to bring us back together
and erase all this pain.</i>

00:22.190 --> 00:23.150
Eva?

00:23.900 --> 00:26.400
<i>At least, that was the plan.</i>

01:45.020 --> 01:46.480
Are you OK?

01:46.730 --> 01:49.190
I can't say that.
But I'm alive.

01:50.030 --> 01:51.570
Yeah, same here.

01:51.740 --> 01:53.200
But how did we get...

02:00.000 --> 02:01.620
It's a total wreck.

02:01.790 --> 02:03.870
What happened to us, Molly?

02:17.050 --> 02:18.470
These walls are...

02:19.100 --> 02:20.970
covered with murals.

02:42.040 --> 02:43.960
Hello?

02:45.210 --> 02:47.290
Anybody there?

02:50.550 --> 02:52.340
I guess not.

02:57.550 --> 03:00.060
Too bad we didn't crash
on a tropical island.

03:22.830 --> 03:24.450
Stan, Koji, are you there?

03:24.580 --> 03:26.580
This is Molly.
Can you hear me?

03:29.250 --> 03:31.130
Molly to Earth team module.

03:31.340 --> 03:33.170
Please come in. Over.

03:33.510 --> 03:35.670
Earth team module, answer me!

03:39.970 --> 03:42.100
<i>Earth team module here.
Do you copy?</i>

03:42.260 --> 03:44.390
Koji, is that you?
Answer me!

03:46.640 --> 03:48.730
Koji. Can you hear me?

03:51.570 --> 03:52.820
Great!

04:00.870 --> 04:02.160
Jordan, what are you doing?

04:02.660 --> 04:04.660
-We're not moving in.
-How do you know?

04:04.830 --> 04:06.540
We may be stuck here
for a long time

04:06.660 --> 04:08.540
before someone
comes to rescue us.

04:17.260 --> 04:20.140
You mean you don't like
our home sweet home?

04:23.140 --> 04:24.180
We're outta here!

04:25.970 --> 04:28.190
What are you talking about?
Are you crazy?

04:28.350 --> 04:30.770
You have no idea
what we could run into!

04:30.980 --> 04:32.360
We might get eaten!

04:36.570 --> 04:38.360
We'll never be found down here.

04:38.740 --> 04:42.030
Our only chance is to get
to the top of these canyons quick.

04:43.120 --> 04:44.450
Come on, let's go.

05:03.930 --> 05:05.810
Did you really have
to bring all that junk?

05:06.310 --> 05:08.730
In a few days you'll be
thanking me for this junk.

05:33.580 --> 05:36.170
Well, what we do now?
Flap our arms and take off?

05:39.920 --> 05:41.420
I don't think we have a choice.

05:41.590 --> 05:43.760
We have to keep going,
no matter what.

05:48.520 --> 05:49.980
Molly, don't be stupid.

05:50.140 --> 05:52.890
Come back here now!
We can still go back to camp.

05:53.020 --> 05:53.980
We'll be safe!

05:54.100 --> 05:56.980
We have water, food,
and... and each other.

06:04.950 --> 06:06.990
<i>I can't give up now.</i>

06:07.200 --> 06:08.950
<i>I have to get back in the race.</i>

06:09.120 --> 06:11.330
<i>I have to win
the Ultimate Prize.</i>

06:14.920 --> 06:17.090
Ay ay ay, the things I do.

06:17.250 --> 06:19.500
Relax, Jordan.
Take a deep breath...

06:21.590 --> 06:24.300
Smile, and think of home.

06:30.520 --> 06:32.180
What is it now? Locusts?

06:35.190 --> 06:36.190
Molly, watch out!

06:42.190 --> 06:42.780
Molly!

07:00.800 --> 07:02.760
Thanks a lot, Jordan.

07:04.840 --> 07:06.340
It was nothing. Really.

07:14.940 --> 07:15.690
Shall we go?

07:27.320 --> 07:29.820
I really thought
I had something, but...

07:30.080 --> 07:33.410
Whatever it was,
all communications are dead.

07:35.290 --> 07:37.000
Try again!

07:37.620 --> 07:39.330
Didn't you hear what I said?

07:39.540 --> 07:41.290
I said keep trying!

07:43.460 --> 07:45.550
<i>Hang on, Eva.</i>

08:19.290 --> 08:20.750
I'm beat.

08:20.920 --> 08:23.000
Doesn't this tunnel ever end?

08:28.260 --> 08:30.140
I wish you still had
your backpack.

08:30.890 --> 08:34.390
Yeah, well, I had a choice
between saving you or the backpack.

08:34.970 --> 08:36.600
I chose to save you.

08:36.770 --> 08:37.520
Sorry.

08:59.540 --> 09:00.830
Daylight, Jordan!

09:01.000 --> 09:02.210
We made it!

09:02.960 --> 09:03.710
Great!

09:15.890 --> 09:17.720
I want my pillow.

09:34.740 --> 09:35.660
Look over there.

09:35.780 --> 09:37.790
There's a big staircase
on the other side.

09:37.950 --> 09:39.750
We're almost there, Jordan.

09:42.620 --> 09:45.000
If we hurry, we might
make it before nightfall.

10:15.120 --> 10:17.740
Hey, Molly?
Why don't we rest a bit?

10:18.490 --> 10:20.950
I don't think I can feel
my legs anymore.

10:23.330 --> 10:26.380
If we stop now, we won't be able
to start again later.

10:55.990 --> 10:57.120
Who's there?

10:57.910 --> 10:58.780
Eva!

11:02.580 --> 11:03.710
It's not possible.

11:11.050 --> 11:13.210
Darling, what's wrong?

11:13.590 --> 11:15.470
You look so tired.

11:15.680 --> 11:17.930
You're pushing yourself too hard.

11:18.300 --> 11:21.390
You need to rest
and take care of yourself.

11:21.640 --> 11:22.680
It's really you.

11:23.140 --> 11:24.140
Mother!

11:28.310 --> 11:29.270
Molly?

11:29.520 --> 11:30.360
Jordan?

11:36.570 --> 11:37.740
Jordan?

11:38.110 --> 11:40.070
There's something
I really need to tell you.

11:43.080 --> 11:46.750
Something I've been meaning
to tell you for a very long time.

11:49.670 --> 11:51.040
Well, then, go ahead.

11:51.920 --> 11:54.510
I feel very close
to you, Jordan.

11:54.840 --> 11:58.430
I've felt this way
since the very first time I saw you.

11:58.720 --> 12:00.350
Are you serious?

12:00.800 --> 12:02.140
That's great.

12:02.350 --> 12:03.260
Fantastic.

12:03.560 --> 12:05.680
I mean, that's exactly
the way I feel.

12:11.150 --> 12:14.570
Molly, I'm so HAPPY-

12:20.820 --> 12:21.700
No!

12:35.000 --> 12:37.010
Hey, Jordan?
What is this place?

12:37.170 --> 12:39.050
I think I'm starting
to see things.

12:39.220 --> 12:40.510
We're just tired.

12:40.590 --> 12:42.970
We're hungry, we're thirsty.
That's all it is.

12:51.520 --> 12:53.650
More hallucinations?
What do they want?

12:54.730 --> 12:56.570
I'm not sticking around
to find out!

14:36.000 --> 14:37.960
I don't like this, Molly.

14:38.130 --> 14:39.630
These murals are
freaking me out.

14:58.900 --> 15:00.900
The symbol of the Avatar.

15:01.110 --> 15:04.530
If this temple is linked to him,
then there may be hope for us yet.

15:04.700 --> 15:06.820
I really want to believe you.

15:47.740 --> 15:49.870
Aw, don't tell me, a dead end?

15:50.030 --> 15:52.330
After all we've been through?
No way!

15:52.910 --> 15:55.290
I want to go home!

15:59.000 --> 16:00.590
I don't know
how to explain it, Jordan,

16:00.750 --> 16:04.170
but I feel we're here
for a reason.

16:04.710 --> 16:07.090
Right. Like starving to death.

16:31.700 --> 16:33.780
The time to award
the Ultimate Prize

16:33.950 --> 16:35.910
has not yet come.

16:36.200 --> 16:39.370
Who dares enter
the Temple of the Heart?

16:39.830 --> 16:40.460
Who?

16:41.040 --> 16:42.920
We are... we are...

16:43.290 --> 16:44.590
We are the Earth team,

16:44.750 --> 16:47.380
finalists
in the Great Race of Oban.

16:48.630 --> 16:50.220
Leave us alone!

16:50.380 --> 16:52.430
And you. Who are you?

16:54.100 --> 16:55.310
We?

16:55.850 --> 16:59.020
It's been so long,
we barely remember.

16:59.350 --> 17:02.900
We are what began,
and what will finish.

17:03.270 --> 17:07.280
We are the fleeting shadows
of a once proud and powerful race.

17:07.440 --> 17:09.650
We are the last of the Creators.

17:09.820 --> 17:11.030
Or what remains of them.

17:11.450 --> 17:12.950
You're not making
any sense at all!

17:13.120 --> 17:14.990
Explain yourselves clearly!

17:15.160 --> 17:18.000
We have no reason
to answer you.

17:18.540 --> 17:22.670
It is beyond
your realm of comprehension.

17:25.340 --> 17:26.840
Why d0l1't you try us?

17:32.010 --> 17:33.010
Very well.

17:33.180 --> 17:34.760
Here is our story.

17:34.970 --> 17:36.890
Understand us if you can.

17:39.100 --> 17:42.230
Where we came from
is of little importance.

17:42.440 --> 17:44.560
What matters
is that we were.

17:45.020 --> 17:47.860
And with us, Oban was created.

17:48.110 --> 17:49.940
Oban, the Mother Planet.

17:50.110 --> 17:52.450
Source of boundless power.

17:53.780 --> 17:56.740
Our most glorious project.

17:58.240 --> 17:59.450
From her womb,

17:59.620 --> 18:02.540
we developed
and created this galaxy.

18:02.790 --> 18:04.630
Planet after planet...

18:04.790 --> 18:07.710
Improving
upon each new creation.

18:08.170 --> 18:09.550
The creators of Oban.

18:09.710 --> 18:12.340
The Creators sending planet seeds
into outer space.

18:13.590 --> 18:16.720
But with immortality
comes frustration.

18:16.890 --> 18:19.430
And with power comes envy.

18:23.810 --> 18:25.520
There were some among us

18:25.690 --> 18:29.480
who wanted to claim
all the power for themselves.

18:29.690 --> 18:34.200
Rivalry and alliances
led to a terrible battle.

18:35.200 --> 18:38.080
Black magic mixed with white.

18:38.370 --> 18:41.660
Forces too powerful
to be unleashed.

18:41.830 --> 18:45.710
In front of this temple,
in the Arena of the Heart,

18:45.880 --> 18:49.630
raged the fiercest battle
since the beginning of Time!

18:58.350 --> 19:02.930
In an instant,
our powerful civilization ceased to be.

19:03.140 --> 19:06.310
And with it,
most of the Galaxy we had created.

19:06.520 --> 19:08.940
To cleanse ourselves
from this horror...

19:09.110 --> 19:10.110
We!

19:10.270 --> 19:11.820
The last survivors,

19:11.980 --> 19:14.820
...renounced
our own immortality.

19:22.870 --> 19:25.870
It was our choice
that the next master of Oban...

19:26.040 --> 19:27.380
and all its power...

19:27.540 --> 19:31.300
would be chosen
among the very planets we had created.

19:31.460 --> 19:33.340
An individual
of great will...

19:33.510 --> 19:35.420
Great strength...

19:35.590 --> 19:38.090
Chosen every 10,000 years...

19:38.260 --> 19:41.470
Through the most daring
competition ever conceived.

19:42.060 --> 19:44.350
This is how
the Great Race of Oban

19:44.520 --> 19:45.850
came into being.

19:46.270 --> 19:49.360
What do you mean,
choosing the master of Oban?

19:50.690 --> 19:51.730
That's impossible!

19:52.190 --> 19:54.820
I want the Ultimate Prize
for my mother!

19:56.030 --> 19:58.240
We answered your question.

19:58.410 --> 20:00.070
Now leave!

20:01.830 --> 20:03.910
No, wait! That can't be!

20:07.870 --> 20:10.130
Do you believe any of this?

20:10.580 --> 20:12.670
I don't know what to think.

20:13.880 --> 20:16.300
Did we even see those Creators?

20:16.420 --> 20:20.430
For all we know, it was
just another... hallucination.

20:20.850 --> 20:23.180
Look, Molly.
It's a magic portal.

20:29.350 --> 20:31.060
Come on.
Let's get out of this place.

20:31.230 --> 20:34.020
Jordan, we have no idea
where this portal will take us.

20:34.190 --> 20:37.780
It could very well be a trap.
Some place much worse than here.

20:39.990 --> 20:41.870
Well, I'll take my chances.

20:43.870 --> 20:45.490
As long as
I'm with you, partner,

20:46.870 --> 20:48.210
everything's gonna be OK.

20:50.420 --> 20:52.290
You're a true friend, Jordan.

20:52.540 --> 20:54.420
And a complete nutcase.

21:11.850 --> 21:13.980
Watch out, Molly.
Stay behind me.

21:22.990 --> 21:24.830
I've seen this place before.

21:24.990 --> 21:27.240
We're in Satis'
secret apartment.

21:27.580 --> 21:30.160
Jordan, we're back
in the Flying Temple!
